/*!

\page arcstk-id

\brief Calculate AccurateRip ids locally

\version @PROJECT_VERSION@



\section id_syno SYNOPSIS

arcstk-id [OPTIONS] TOCFILE [AUDIOFILE1 AUDIOFILE2 ...]


\section id_desc DESCRIPTION

Calculate the AccurateRip id of an album by its metadata or by audio data.

The track offsets and the leadout offset are required to calculate the
AccurateRip id. Some metadata formats like Cuesheet do not include the leadout
offset. In this case, the actual audio data must be inspected to acquire this
information.

If the metadata file contains the name of an audio file, this audio file is
used. Option \b -a allows to specify the audio file explicitly in case the file
name is not present in the metadata or intended to be overridden.

This calculation may fail for discs with data tracks or pregap tracks.


\section id_opts OPTIONS


\subsection id_opts_in  Options for Input

\par -a, \--audiofile=FILEPATH
Specify a single audio file to read the leadout offset. This overrides any audio
filename that may be present in the metadata.

\snippet{doc} include/option_listaudioformats.dox  OPT_LISTAUDIOFORMATS

\snippet{doc} include/option_listtocformats.dox    OPT_LISTTOCFORMATS


\subsection id_opts_out Options for Output

\par \--cddb-id
Print the CDDB id of the album.

\par \--db-id, \--filename
Print the AccurateRip database id. This id is identical to the canonical
filename of the AccurateRip response file and has the following format of 38
characters length:
<tt>dBAR-<track_count:3>-<id1:8>-<id2:8>-<cddb_id:8>.bin</tt>.

\snippet{doc} include/option_help.dox      OPT_HELP

\snippet{doc} include/option_logfile.dox   OPT_LOGFILE

\par \--no-labels
Suppress output of labels when using \b --profile or any combination of
\b --cddb-id, \b --db-id, and \b --url.

\snippet{doc} include/option_outfile.dox   OPT_OUTFILE

\snippet{doc} include/option_parser.dox    OPT_PARSER

\par \--profile
Print all information as a table.

\snippet{doc} include/option_quiet.dox     OPT_QUIET

\snippet{doc} include/option_reader.dox    OPT_READER

\par \--url
Print the AccurateRip request url.

\par \--url-prefix=STRING
Use a custom url prefix for url output. The default prefix is
<tt>http://accuraterip.com/accuraterip/</tt>. If the custom prefix does not end
with a slash, a trailing slash '/' is appended automatically.

\snippet{doc} include/option_verbosity.dox OPT_VERBOSITY

\snippet{doc} include/option_version.dox   OPT_VERSION


\section id_exmp EXAMPLES

Compute AccurateRip id for audiofile.cue while having the real audio file in the
same directory:

\code{.sh}$ arcstk-id audiofile.cue\endcode

Do the same as in the first example, but track precisely what is going on:

\code{.sh}$ arcstk-id --vvv audiofile.cue\endcode


\section id_bugs BUGS

\snippet{doc} include/text_bugs.dox    TEXT_BUGS


\section id_copy COPYRIGHT

\snippet{doc} include/text_license.dox TEXT_LICENSE


\section id_see SEE ALSO

@TOOL_NAME_CALC@(1), @TOOL_NAME_PARSE@(1), @TOOL_NAME_VERIFY@(1)

*/
